INSERT INTO transcript (conversation_id, item_id, seq, role, text, complete, at, copied_at, compaction) VALUES (1, 'toolu_01UZHCC156jvCwnrnd7osSxX', 64, 'tool', '1	<!doctype html>
2	<html lang="en">
3	<head>
4	  <meta charset="utf-8">
5	  <title>Frequently Asked Questions — Burnout at Work</title>
6	  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css">
7	</head>
8	<body>
9	  <header>
10	    <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
11	    <nav><a href="index.html">Home</a> · <a href="assessment.html">Assessment</a> · <a href="../faq.html">RO</a></nav>
12	  </header>
13	  <main>
14	    <section class="faq">
15	      <details>
16	        <summary><strong>Who can participate in the assessment?</strong></summary>
17	        <p>Any team in any company, regardless of size. The programme is designed to be scalable—it works just as well for a small team of 5 people as for an organization with hundreds of employees. The only requirement: the team should have at least one person to complete the questionnaire.</p>
18	      </details>
19	
20	      <details>
21	        <summary><strong>How long does the assessment take?</strong></summary>
22	        <p>The questionnaire takes approximately 20 minutes. Any employee can complete it at work, during breaks, or after hours. No special preparation or prior documentation is needed.</p>
23	      </details>
24	
25	      <details>
26	        <summary><strong>Is it truly anonymous? What happens with the data?</strong></summary>
27	        <p>Yes, the assessment is completely anonymous. Individual responses are never visible—not to managers, not to HR. This protects each employee''s privacy and encourages honest answers.</p>
28	        <p>Aggregate data (the team''s colour and score) is stored securely and used only for assessment and improvement purposes. It is never sold, shared with third parties, or used for commercial purposes. Only the team-level result is visible to the manager and HR.</p>
29	      </details>
30	
31	      <details>
32	        <summary><strong>What if a team doesn''t like the results?</strong></summary>
33	        <p>The results are a starting point, not a verdict. If a team has a high burnout score, the goal is to understand the causes and take action. The manager and team can have an open discussion about what is causing stress and how to reduce it.</p>
34	        <p>The recommendations in the report are concrete and action-oriented—they provide specific directions for improvement. Many teams find that simply addressing the issue systematically leads to positive changes right away.</p>
35	      </details>
36	
37	      <details>
38	        <summary><strong>What happens after the assessment? What''s the timeline?</strong></summary>
39	        <p>Once the team completes the questionnaire, results are calculated within hours. The manager receives the report with the colour, score, and specific recommendations.</p>
40	        <p>Within the following week, the manager discusses the results with the team—not as a punishment, but as an open conversation about wellbeing and identifying areas for improvement. This discussion is critical: it turns data into concrete action.</p>
41	        <p>After that, it depends on the team how they want to proceed. Some implement changes right away; others plan over the medium term.</p>
42	      </details>
43	
44	      <details>
45	        <summary><strong>How are the colours and scores determined?</strong></summary>
46	        <p>The score (0–100) is calculated based on responses to three main dimensions of burnout:</p>
47	        <ul>
48	          <li><strong>Exhaustion:</strong> physical and emotional fatigue</li>
49	          <li><strong>Cynicism:</strong> detachment or negativity toward work</li>
50	          <li><strong>Reduced professional efficacy:</strong> a sense of lower performance and diminished significance</li>
51	        </ul>
52	        <p>The colours (green, yellow, orange, red) are assigned based on this score and indicate the level of burnout risk. This is a recognized standard in occupational psychology and provides a reliable picture of team wellbeing.</p>
53	      </details>
54	
55	      <details>
56	        <summary><strong>Can individual employees see their own score?</strong></summary>
57	        <p>No. Results are team-level only, not individual. This is intentional: it protects anonymity and avoids creating the impression that any one person is "the problem". If someone from the team is particularly affected, the manager can invite them to a one-on-one support conversation, but raw data is not exposed.</p>
58	      </details>
59	    </section>
60	  </main>
61	  <footer>
62	    <nav>
63	      <a href="about.html">About us</a> · <a href="faq.html">FAQ</a> · <a href="contact.html">Contact</a>
64	    </nav>
65	  </footer>
66	</body>
67	</html>
68	', 1, '2026-10-31T16:06:50.516Z', '2026-10-31T16:06:50.653Z', 0);
